WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.425
The average person checks
 email 74 times a day,

00:00:03.425 --> 00:00:05.816
and switches tasks 
on their computer

00:00:05.816 --> 00:00:09.580
566 times a day.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.792
Researchers at USC 
have found --

00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:14.455
they're&nbsp;studying teenagers 
who are on social media

00:00:14.455 --> 00:00:15.653
while they're talking
 to their friends

00:00:15.653 --> 00:00:17.214
or they're&nbsp;doing
homework,

00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:18.588
and two years 
down the road,

00:00:18.588 --> 00:00:21.213
they are less creative 
and imaginative

00:00:21.213 --> 00:00:23.127
about their&nbsp;own 
personal futures

00:00:23.127 --> 00:00:25.292
and about solving 
societal problems.

00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:27.602
So the next time you go
to check your&nbsp;phone,

00:00:27.602 --> 00:00:30.621
ask yourself: What am
 I really looking for?

00:00:30.621 --> 00:00:32.000
Because if it's 
to check email,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.882
that's fine&nbsp;-- do 
it and be done.

00:00:34.105 --> 00:00:35.509
But if it's to 
distract yourself

00:00:35.509 --> 00:00:36.765
from doing the hard work

00:00:36.765 --> 00:00:38.462
that comes&nbsp;with 
deeper thinking,

00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:40.471
take a break,

00:00:40.471 --> 00:00:41.865
stare out the window

00:00:41.865 --> 00:00:44.888
and know that 
by doing nothing

00:00:44.888 --> 00:00:47.660
you are&nbsp;actually being 
your most productive

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.425
and creative self.

00:00:49.425 --> 00:00:51.022
It might feel weird 
and uncomfortable

00:00:51.022 --> 00:00:53.375
at&nbsp;first, but 
boredom

00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:55.647
truly can lead 
to brilliance.

